  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "His Demon Venerable soul has a thousand arms and palms and three heads. The front head has dragon horns, a lion mane, snake eyes, and elephant tusks. The left head has a peach forehead, grass hair, and three flower-like eyes. The right head has a cloud fringe, lightning eyes, fire ears, and a golden mouth. Southern Border mortals use clay to make statues of this form, to pray to and give offerings.",
      "chapters": [
        443
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His soul path foundation is so deep it reaches the limits of a material state, which is why his ghostly hand behaves like something solid rather than incorporeal.",
      "chapters": [
        1010
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-path-foundation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "His soul stands thousands of meters tall, like an imposing giant. Dark clouds reach only his waist. His leg resembles a giant mountain peak, and his chest reaches the clouds. He has a thousand arms, five hundred on each side, dark like ink, with bulging muscles and firm lines. He also has a thousand ghostly hands.",
      "chapters": [
        1011
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yi-tian-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He has disheveled hair. His hands and body are covered in blood. He is skinny like a skeleton. His eyes are deeply swollen and shine with brilliant light.",
      "chapters": [
        1015
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "secret-room",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a pale face and chest-length hair.",
      "chapters": [
        1969
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-heaven",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Young Spectral Soul, Ming You, wears a black robe.",
      "chapters": [
        2055
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "qing-clan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He opens his eyes. The two blood suns let out ominous light from the dark cloudy fog.",
      "chapters": [
        2193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "face",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 422 carries his name as its entire title, near the end of the Hu Immortal Blessed Land stretch. That chapter also calls him the Gu Immortal with the greatest killing nature.",
      "chapters": [
        422
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "where-he-enters-the-story",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The chapter that first puts his name on the page also names Dang Hun Mountain and Luo Po Valley as the two sacred lands of soul path Gu Masters, one for strengthening and one for refining.",
      "chapters": [
        422
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_dang_hun_mountain",
        "loc_luo_po_valley",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Northern Plains chapter measuring a weaker soul against his record calls him the number one soul cultivator in history and states that he surpassed hundred million man soul.",
      "chapters": [
        443
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-cultivation-record",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later chapter places him at the apex of rank nine peak stage.",
      "chapters": [
        508
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-cultivation-record",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soul path Gu worms had appeared since the immemorial era without forming a path. Only upon his rise did the path form and flourish, and he singlehandedly pushed it to its peak over history. During his era, out of ten Gu Masters, at least five chose to cultivate soul path. History also names him the venerable with the most murderous nature, because creating soul path Gu worms drove endless slaughter for souls.",
      "chapters": [
        996
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-history",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "path_soul",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Demon Venerable names a rank nine demonic path Gu Master; Immortal Venerable names a rank nine righteous Gu Master.",
      "chapters": [
        383
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
